    {
      "id": "s02-carrier",
      "intent": "The carrier equation separates dense feature creation from token partitioning, and the window step keeps the feature field as the represented content.",
      "claim": "\\mathbf{F}=\\mathcal{E}(\\mathbf{I}_{\\mathrm{LR}}),\\qquad \\mathbf{X}=\\mathcal{W}(\\mathbf{F})",
      "narration": "The encoder maps the low-resolution image into a dense feature field named F. The window operator then partitions that field, and the tokens are X rather than a discarded summary. The repeated F shows that the window step keeps the dense carrier as the source of every token.",
